 Rail setup      │
                 │  Register Rail with your provider
 ✓ Start         │
 ✓ Provider      │  1. In Google Cloud Console create a project and enable the Gmail API.                            ▲
 ▸ Instructions  │  2. OAuth consent screen: choose External, then set the publishing status to "In production". An  █
   Details       │  app left in Testing expires refresh tokens after 7 days.                                         █
 – Admin consent │  3. Credentials: create an OAuth client ID of type Desktop app.                                   █
   Login         │  4. Copy the client ID and the client secret into the next step.                                  █
   Done          │                                                                                                   █
                 │  Scope Rail asks for:                                                                             █
                 │  https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.modify                                                     █
                 │                                                                                                   █
                 │  Redirect URI: Desktop app clients accept http://127.0.0.1 on any port; there is nothing to add.  █
